WEBVTT

00:03.160 --> 00:05.900
Go, Eren!

00:14.150 --> 00:15.760
In the year 850...

00:16.610 --> 00:18.679
For the first time,

00:18.680 --> 00:21.840
humanity recovered part of its
territory from the Titans.

00:23.220 --> 00:25.530
Though at great cost.

00:28.050 --> 00:33.300
Then I welcome everyone
here to the Survey Corps!

00:33.700 --> 00:35.640
This is a true salute!

00:36.010 --> 00:37.390
Offer up your hearts!

00:39.260 --> 00:40.320
Yes, sir!

00:44.430 --> 00:46.660
You have done well to endure your fear.

00:47.480 --> 00:49.570
You are brave soldiers.

00:50.310 --> 00:51.980
You have my heartfelt respect.

00:53.690 --> 00:54.990
A month later,

00:55.750 --> 00:59.039
led by Erwin Smith, the
Survey Corps left Karanes

00:59.040 --> 01:01.489
to find a route to Zhiganshina,

01:01.490 --> 01:06.540
where it's believed the secrets
of the Titans are held.

01:12.110 --> 01:15.300
We will now begin the 57th
expedition beyond the walls!

01:16.390 --> 01:18.140
Onward!

01:21.610 --> 01:22.970
Oh, my friend!

01:22.970 --> 01:25.490
This is a victory for us!

01:25.550 --> 01:28.650
Our fame starts here!

01:28.690 --> 01:29.750
Oh, my friend!

01:29.750 --> 01:34.950
Let us celebrate this victory for the next battle!

01:49.590 --> 01:55.130
"I died for naught"
I won't let it end like that for you

01:55.130 --> 02:00.390
until I am the last one standing

02:00.390 --> 02:03.370
The enemy is cruel... We will kill...

02:03.370 --> 02:06.410
The enemy is colossal... We will jump...

02:06.410 --> 02:10.050
In our hands we hold blades of glory

02:10.050 --> 02:12.330
and sing in the name of victory

02:12.330 --> 02:16.970
We bear the wings of freedom on our backs

02:18.290 --> 02:24.410
Swearing iron determination upon our hearts,

02:24.430 --> 02:28.950
we slash apart the circle of idiocy

02:30.530 --> 02:32.850
and soar through the sky

02:32.910 --> 02:37.110
with our wings of freedom

02:51.020 --> 02:55.980
Female Titan: The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 1

03:16.060 --> 03:18.380
Ahead, to the left, a 10-meter class!

03:18.750 --> 03:22.260
I am very interested in seeing
what's inside its stomach...

03:22.990 --> 03:24.760
But I'll leave it to the support team!

03:28.130 --> 03:28.890
Damn!

03:29.350 --> 03:30.390
Not deep enough.

03:31.180 --> 03:32.900
Defend the formation!

03:37.150 --> 03:38.440
Stay strong!

03:38.640 --> 03:40.830
Leave it to the support
team, and keep going!

03:43.110 --> 03:46.950
Onward! Onward!

03:52.030 --> 03:54.960
The support teams will only
accompany us to the old city area.

03:55.310 --> 03:58.400
Once we're past that,
it's completely Titan territory.

03:58.800 --> 04:04.220
The long-range scouting formation devised
by Commander Erwin is our only hope.

04:04.920 --> 04:07.610
We, the special ops squad, are here.

04:10.230 --> 04:12.260
Sir, can they...

04:13.020 --> 04:15.150
Can my classmates beat the Titans?

04:15.570 --> 04:16.520
Huh?

04:16.521 --> 04:19.670
What have you been doing the past month?

04:20.990 --> 04:22.939
Listen, brat...

04:22.940 --> 04:24.699
The most crucial part

04:24.700 --> 04:27.320
of an expedition is in how
you avoid fighting Titans

04:35.720 --> 04:38.170
Go into long-range scouting formation!

04:40.220 --> 04:41.680
See ya, Armin.

04:42.480 --> 04:45.050
If you run into a Titan,
don't piss your pants!

04:45.610 --> 04:46.639
Right!

04:46.640 --> 04:47.780
Same to you, Jean.

04:54.406 --> 04:55.916
Row 3-3: Relay

04:55.941 --> 04:57.550
The vanguard is to spread
out in a semi-circle.

04:57.575 --> 05:01.215
But stay within visual
range of one another.

05:01.240 --> 05:02.760
Row 5-Center: Standby

05:02.785 --> 05:04.585
Position yourselves at fixed intervals.

05:04.610 --> 05:08.670
Extend the recon and message relay
range as far as possible.

05:33.240 --> 05:34.280
We'll be fine...

05:34.590 --> 05:35.610
Calm down!

05:40.060 --> 05:44.660
It's primarily the forward recon squad
that will encounter Titans.

05:51.160 --> 05:55.700
As soon as one is sighted,
they'll fire a red smoke round.

05:58.860 --> 06:03.110
Anyone who sees the flare should fire
the same round to relay the signal.

06:06.940 --> 06:10.179
When the Commander sees it,

06:10.180 --> 06:12.140
he'll fire a green smoke round,

06:13.670 --> 06:16.770
and show the formation where to go.

06:18.770 --> 06:23.519
Thus, the entire formation can advance

06:23.520 --> 06:25.860
toward the goal, while avoiding Titans.

06:28.640 --> 06:32.989
But sometimes, due to terrain or obstacles,

06:32.990 --> 06:36.120
a Titan won't be sighted until
it's within the formation.

06:42.890 --> 06:44.459
Red... Red...

06:44.460 --> 06:45.920
Red smoke round...

06:50.120 --> 06:51.800
Blause! Over here!

06:54.190 --> 06:56.669
Damn it! Did we let one through?

06:56.670 --> 06:58.060
We'll draw it this way.

06:58.570 --> 07:00.440
Blause, get over here!

07:11.260 --> 07:12.240
I'll handle it!

07:12.240 --> 07:13.190
Split off!

07:13.190 --> 07:14.160
Yes, sir!

07:32.460 --> 07:33.719
Sir...

07:33.720 --> 07:35.010
Back into position!

07:35.280 --> 07:36.770
He ran out of gas.

07:42.020 --> 07:43.610
Something's wrong...

07:43.940 --> 07:46.369
It's been a while since we
saw the red smoke round,

07:46.370 --> 07:47.980
but they still haven't reformed.

07:48.470 --> 07:49.490
It can't be...

07:50.690 --> 07:53.909
Note that this strategy only
works on normal Titans,

07:53.910 --> 07:57.240
whose behavior can be easily predicted.

08:00.160 --> 08:01.660
A black smoke round?

08:02.290 --> 08:04.009
Is a Titan ignoring the nearby humans

08:04.010 --> 08:06.210
and heading for the formation's center?

08:06.960 --> 08:08.000
It has to be...

08:08.450 --> 08:09.590
That's

08:10.880 --> 08:12.190
an Aberrant!

08:13.870 --> 08:16.849
It's only necessary to fight Aberrants,

08:16.850 --> 08:18.509
whose behavior is unpredictable.

08:18.510 --> 08:21.099
Damn, we'll have to fight it...

08:21.100 --> 08:22.940
Sys, go for the neck!

08:23.480 --> 08:24.899
I'll stop it!

08:24.900 --> 08:26.230
Roger!

08:28.130 --> 08:31.319
Using Maneuver Gear on flat
terrain is a huge disadvantage.

08:31.320 --> 08:33.320
It almost never works.

08:33.680 --> 08:36.480
But I can't let it disrupt the formation.

08:37.350 --> 08:39.979
I think that's Arlert over there.

08:39.980 --> 08:42.810
I don't want one of the
new guys to run into it.

08:43.210 --> 08:44.370
We kill it here!

08:52.950 --> 08:54.130
Now, Sys!

09:01.140 --> 09:03.270
You did it, Squad Leader Ness!

09:06.030 --> 09:07.190
Did I get him?

09:09.110 --> 09:10.429
You came for me?

09:10.430 --> 09:12.370
That's my partner...

09:13.210 --> 09:15.670
I love you, Shallot!

09:23.970 --> 09:24.990
Again?

09:25.370 --> 09:27.959
What is the right flank recon squad doing?

09:27.960 --> 09:29.869
If it ignored them and came this way,

09:29.870 --> 09:31.620
it must be another Aberrant.

09:32.490 --> 09:33.940
Oh, fine...

09:35.080 --> 09:37.009
Sys, we do it again.

09:37.010 --> 09:37.800
Right.

09:38.760 --> 09:42.310
But we've got the worst luck,
doing this twice in a row...

09:42.860 --> 09:45.370
And I think it's at least
a fourteen-meter class.

09:45.720 --> 09:47.390
This one will be tough.

09:57.000 --> 09:58.209
What's that?

09:58.210 --> 09:59.370
It's too fast!

09:59.570 --> 10:01.329
Don't let it reach Arlert!

10:01.330 --> 10:02.030
Sys!

10:02.530 --> 10:03.570
Right!

10:37.950 --> 10:40.280
No... No.

10:40.740 --> 10:41.920
That's no Aberrant.

10:42.270 --> 10:43.620
It's intelligent!

10:44.040 --> 10:46.850
Like the Armored or
Colossal Titans, or Eren...

10:47.450 --> 10:49.830
A human in the body of a Titan!

10:50.370 --> 10:51.330
B-But who?

10:51.920 --> 10:52.840
Why?

10:53.320 --> 10:54.800
This is bad! What should I do?

10:54.960 --> 10:55.969
I'm going to die, too...

10:55.970 --> 10:56.880
I'll be killed!

10:58.610 --> 11:00.380
Go! Run!

11:07.870 --> 11:09.310
What does it...

11:11.580 --> 11:13.810
No, what do they...

11:17.110 --> 11:18.980
What do they want?

11:33.220 --> 11:35.050
Someone tell them...

11:36.150 --> 11:40.170
That the right flank recon squad
has been wiped out...

11:40.850 --> 11:45.450
A Female Titan brought
a huge Titan army!

11:47.030 --> 11:49.560
Is anyone there?

12:47.900 --> 12:50.160
It's not going to kill me?

12:50.620 --> 12:51.840
Why?

12:53.040 --> 12:55.040
It removed my hood...

12:55.420 --> 12:59.740
To... To look at my face?

13:00.430 --> 13:01.310
Armin!

13:02.520 --> 13:03.570
Reiner!

13:04.440 --> 13:06.300
Hey, can you stand?

13:07.040 --> 13:11.590
You won't last outside the walls
unless you're on horseback...

13:11.590 --> 13:12.590
Hurry!

13:12.590 --> 13:13.630
Right!

13:15.870 --> 13:18.520
I saw the smoke round
signaling an Aberrant.

13:18.520 --> 13:20.970
Was it that one there with the nice ass?

13:20.970 --> 13:22.550
That's no Aberrant...

13:22.550 --> 13:24.600
It's a human in a Titan body!

13:24.920 --> 13:26.100
What was that?

13:27.210 --> 13:28.370
Wait a second.

13:28.370 --> 13:29.900
We need to fire a smoke round first.

13:30.260 --> 13:31.500
H-Hurry...

13:31.750 --> 13:33.550
There's an emergency over there.

13:34.030 --> 13:35.110
With a smoke round, I'll...

13:36.210 --> 13:39.330
Wait... I think Jean fired it.

13:42.370 --> 13:44.440
It came from the right flank.

13:44.440 --> 13:47.290
Does that mean we're so compromised,
we can't continue the mission?

13:47.750 --> 13:50.590
Looks like the right flank recon
squad was partially wiped out...

13:50.590 --> 13:52.680
Titans, tons of them.

13:52.680 --> 13:53.920
I don't know why,

13:54.580 --> 13:57.050
but there are lots of fast ones.

13:57.050 --> 13:58.860
For now, we're holding them back,

13:58.860 --> 14:00.760
but recon is no longer possible...

14:01.200 --> 14:02.870
We've taken heavy losses,

14:02.870 --> 14:04.670
and if we aren't careful,
we'll be destroyed!

14:05.240 --> 14:07.310
That Titan came from the same direction.

14:07.870 --> 14:08.730
No way...

14:09.230 --> 14:11.410
Was it leading the Titans?

14:11.820 --> 14:13.030
It?

14:13.640 --> 14:16.030
Why is a Titan over there?

14:16.570 --> 14:17.500
An Aberrant?

14:17.820 --> 14:23.500
No, it's a human in a Titan body...

14:23.500 --> 14:25.620
Someone with the same ability as Eren.

14:25.990 --> 14:27.370
What?

14:27.680 --> 14:30.060
Why do you think that, Armin?

14:31.280 --> 14:33.840
The Titans only eat us.

14:34.270 --> 14:36.520
We're just killed in the process.

14:36.520 --> 14:38.800
Killing us isn't ever
specifically their goal.

14:39.290 --> 14:42.060
But when Sys aimed for its weak spot,

14:42.600 --> 14:45.520
it crushed him and smashed
him into the ground.

14:47.030 --> 14:50.340
It killed him to kill,
rather than to eat him.

14:50.780 --> 14:53.070
Its nature is different from the others.

14:53.730 --> 14:57.630
When the Colossal and Armored
Titans destroyed the walls,

14:57.630 --> 15:01.330
it must've been the one that
brought that army of Titans.

15:01.930 --> 15:05.130
Their goal has consistently
been to attack all humanity!

15:06.880 --> 15:08.580
No, maybe not.

15:09.180 --> 15:11.720
It felt like it was looking for someone...

15:12.200 --> 15:14.970
If that is the case,
could it be looking for...

15:15.910 --> 15:17.760
Could it be looking for Eren?

15:18.130 --> 15:19.800
Eren?

15:19.800 --> 15:24.300
Eren's with Squad Levi, which is
in charge of the right flank.

15:24.950 --> 15:26.230
The right flank?

15:26.860 --> 15:30.870
The plans I got had them
to the rear of the left flank.

15:32.050 --> 15:36.800
Mine said they were near
the front of the right...

15:37.260 --> 15:40.240
Wait, there's no way they'd
be on the front lines.

15:40.640 --> 15:43.120
So where are they?

15:43.570 --> 15:46.800
Probably the safest place in the formation.

15:47.880 --> 15:51.790
Which means in the center,
and toward the rear...

15:52.420 --> 15:53.250
Armin!

15:53.610 --> 15:56.010
There's no time to think.

15:56.280 --> 15:59.510
Smoke rounds can't possibly indicate
how much of a threat it poses!

16:00.100 --> 16:02.530
At this rate, it'll wipe out command.

16:02.530 --> 16:05.740
Then the formation will fall apart,
and that'll be the end.

16:05.740 --> 16:07.100
What are you trying to say?

16:07.510 --> 16:08.960
In other words,

16:08.960 --> 16:11.830
at this range, we may still be
able to draw its attention.

16:12.360 --> 16:15.550
We may be able to buy time to withdraw.

16:16.110 --> 16:19.280
Maybe... Maybe...

16:21.480 --> 16:23.990
But it really is intelligent.

16:24.290 --> 16:27.950
To it, we are nothing but
insignificant insects.

16:27.950 --> 16:30.040
It'll just crush us...

16:30.360 --> 16:31.560
Seriously?

16:32.970 --> 16:34.540
That's scary...

16:34.830 --> 16:37.830
Hey, are you really Jean?

16:37.830 --> 16:42.050
The Jean I know never thinks
of anyone but himself.

16:42.720 --> 16:44.590
Don't be an ass...

16:46.640 --> 16:51.350
I just don't want those charred bones I saw

16:51.840 --> 16:53.840
to be disappointed in me!

16:54.290 --> 16:56.640
I...

16:57.210 --> 17:00.040
I know what I have to do now!

17:00.380 --> 17:03.300
And this is the job we chose.

17:03.300 --> 17:04.490
Help me!

17:10.180 --> 17:11.690
Put on your hood.

17:11.690 --> 17:12.810
As far forward as you can...

17:12.810 --> 17:14.830
So that your face is hidden from it.

17:15.170 --> 17:19.780
I don't think it will kill us until
it knows who we are!

17:19.780 --> 17:20.960
Oh...

17:21.410 --> 17:24.770
You believe if it thinks we might
be Eren, it won't kill us?

17:25.230 --> 17:27.350
If nothing else, it'll make me feel better.

17:27.350 --> 17:30.470
Let's just hope it has poor eyesight!

17:31.280 --> 17:36.710
Armin, I thought it was creepy
how you always clung to Eren.

17:37.150 --> 17:38.830
But I've always thought you had it in you.

17:40.050 --> 17:41.570
Uh, thanks.

17:42.110 --> 17:44.820
But "creepy"? That's really mean...

17:59.590 --> 18:02.170
It's going much more slowly
than when I first saw it.

18:02.590 --> 18:03.730
Is it tired?

18:04.530 --> 18:07.150
If it runs at that speed
again, we'll be too late!

18:07.540 --> 18:10.390
Now's our chance... We have to do it now!

18:16.540 --> 18:19.520
Listen up... Remember what I said.

18:20.310 --> 18:22.800
Try to draw its attention
for as long as possible,

18:22.800 --> 18:25.170
to give the formation time to withdraw!

18:25.170 --> 18:27.380
Keep it here as long as you can.

18:28.410 --> 18:31.530
If we could cut its Achilles tendon,
that'd be more than enough.

18:31.850 --> 18:34.450
But don't do anything stupid...

18:34.450 --> 18:35.850
Don't try to kill it!

18:36.350 --> 18:39.080
It's aware of the weak spot on its neck.

18:39.450 --> 18:41.850
It's totally different than other Titans...

18:41.850 --> 18:43.440
It is impossible to kill.

18:43.870 --> 18:48.070
At least, not by any normal human being.

18:51.460 --> 18:52.430
However...

18:52.430 --> 18:54.690
If it's those two... Maybe...

19:36.040 --> 19:36.900
Armin!

19:39.360 --> 19:40.510
This one...

19:40.510 --> 19:42.810
Its movements are much more
precise than the others' are!

19:42.810 --> 19:43.900
Damn it.

19:43.900 --> 19:44.990
I...

19:45.270 --> 19:47.160
I underestimated it!

19:52.360 --> 19:54.130
It protected its neck...

19:54.400 --> 19:55.090
Jean!

19:56.690 --> 19:58.960
Damn it! I can't get away!

19:59.300 --> 20:00.220
I'm going to die!

20:00.740 --> 20:02.590
Once it grasps my wire, it's over!

20:06.010 --> 20:07.020
Jean!

20:07.020 --> 20:10.010
Avenge the bastard who rushed to his death!

20:11.520 --> 20:12.510
Armin?

20:13.540 --> 20:15.210
It stopped?

20:15.760 --> 20:16.790
That's the one...

20:16.790 --> 20:18.540
That's the one that killed him!

20:18.540 --> 20:21.340
He rushed to his death on the right flank!

20:21.340 --> 20:23.730
Avenge him!

20:28.933 --> 20:29.888
What happened?

20:31.760 --> 20:33.688
Did Armin hit his head and go insane?

20:33.690 --> 20:35.192
This isn't the time...

20:37.355 --> 20:38.333
R-Reiner?

20:39.520 --> 20:42.370
It crushed my best friend!

20:42.630 --> 20:45.330
I saw his body under its foot!

20:48.200 --> 20:50.210
He's going straight for the neck?

20:50.400 --> 20:51.880
No, it's working!

20:51.880 --> 20:54.550
While it's distracted by Armin!

21:02.430 --> 21:04.260
H-Hey...

21:17.250 --> 21:20.690
H-Hey... Reiner, you...

21:37.810 --> 21:40.050
Reiner did it!

21:40.380 --> 21:42.710
Mikasa was so strong, I forgot.

21:42.710 --> 21:45.890
But he's really strong and reliable, too...

21:46.720 --> 21:48.820
We've bought enough time, right?

21:48.820 --> 21:50.480
Let's get the hell away from it!

21:51.080 --> 21:54.730
If it isn't a man-eater,
it won't follow us!

22:03.140 --> 22:04.190
Look...

22:04.190 --> 22:08.490
That big bitch got scared
and decided to go home!

22:09.830 --> 22:11.330
No... Why?

22:12.010 --> 22:14.070
That's toward the center rear.

22:14.640 --> 22:15.650
Is it

22:16.360 --> 22:18.080
heading toward Eren?

22:36.200 --> 22:41.590
If we suppose that I am not me,

22:41.590 --> 22:46.130
Can you say with certainty that you are you?

22:46.780 --> 22:51.660
Will you be able to pick up after yourself

22:51.660 --> 22:56.810
Once your sand-like shell breaks and your heart crumbles?

22:57.090 --> 23:02.020
I could hear someone calling

23:02.310 --> 23:05.920
But now my ears are just ringing

23:06.240 --> 23:11.080
It's as if time has frozen

23:11.380 --> 23:13.990
Now, wake up

23:13.990 --> 23:18.960
I began to walk through a deep dark abyss

23:19.510 --> 23:24.260
As swift as a gale, I escaped for my life

23:24.670 --> 23:28.830
I felt like a living corpse

23:29.240 --> 23:33.960
We break out of our walls

23:34.270 --> 23:40.350
To reunite in worlds we've yet to map

23:53.453 --> 23:54.537
"You damn monster!"

23:55.777 --> 24:00.200
Not even the highly experienced Survey Corps soldiers can stop the female Titan.

24:01.170 --> 24:05.510
And so, the monster finally spots Eren in a forest of giant trees.

24:05.510 --> 24:06.066
Forest of Giant Trees: The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 2
And so, the monster finally spots Eren in a forest of giant trees.

24:06.066 --> 24:07.092
Forest of Giant Trees: The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 2
